; lib_networking/netcode: a game played on several computers, the
; author's playground's libs/networking/netcode (and its protocols'
; Wire and Transport): Wire (a message's bytes), Inputs (the inputs
; exchanged, their acks and checksums), Lockstep (wait for every
; input), Rollback (guess, and replay), Checksum, Sim_net (a network
; in one program, from a seed); Transport, where a peer's packets go:
; here over Udp (ix_tcp), Linux's sockets or Plan 9's /net/udp. Under
; lib_playground/apis's Multiplayer.
